Thinking: We need to answer using the maplibre-cartography skill. Provide code example for smooth flyTo, handling button click, maybe easing, options like center, zoom, bearing, pitch, duration, curve, essential. Also mention that for accessibility, ensure focus, etc. Provide explanation. Use best practices.

Below is a **complete, production‑ready recipe** for “fly the camera to a new place” when the user clicks a button in a MapLibre GL JS map.

It follows the cartographic best‑practice guidelines from the **maplibre‑cartography** skill:

* **Smooth, predictable motion** – use `flyTo` (not `jumpTo`) so the map stays oriented and the user can keep their mental map of the scene.  
* **Easing & duration** – the default curve (`0.25`) and a 1 s duration work well on most devices, but you can tweak them for a tighter or more leisurely feel.  
* **Preserve figure‑ground** – the camera keeps the same pitch/tilt unless you explicitly change them, so any labels or symbols you have styled for imagery stay readable.  
* **Accessibility** – move keyboard focus to the button after the animation and announce the change with an ARIA live region (optional but recommended).

---

## 1️⃣ HTML – a button that triggers the fly

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre flyTo demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; height:100%; }
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
    .control {
      position: absolute;
      top: 10px; left: 10px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.9);
      padding: 6px 10px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<div class="control">
  <button id="flyBtn">Fly to San Francisco</button>
  <!-- optional live‑region for screen‑readers -->
  <div id="flyStatus" aria-live="polite" style="position:absolute; left:-9999px;"></div>
</div>

<script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<script src="fly.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

*The button lives in a small floating panel so it’s always reachable, even on a full‑screen map.*

---

## 2️⃣ JavaScript – map creation + fly logic (`fly.js`)

```js
// ---------------------------------------------------
// 1️⃣ Initialise the map (replace with your own style/tiles)
// ---------------------------------------------------
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json', // or your own style URL
  center: [-122.447303, 37.753574], // initial view (San Francisco)
  zoom: 12,
  pitch: 45,               // keep a modest 3‑D tilt – works well with imagery
  bearing: 0,
  antialias: true
});

// ---------------------------------------------------
// 2️⃣ Helper: smooth fly options (tweak as you like)
// ---------------------------------------------------
function getFlyOptions(target) {
  // `target` = {center: [lon, lat], zoom?: number, bearing?: number, pitch?: number}
  return {
    center: target.center,
    zoom: target.zoom ?? map.getZoom(),          // keep current zoom if not supplied
    bearing: target.bearing ?? map.getBearing(),
    pitch: target.pitch ?? map.getPitch(),
    // Animation curve (0 = linear, 1 = very eased). 0.25 is the MapLibre default.
    curve: 0.25,
    // How long the animation lasts (ms). 1000 ms = 1 s.
    duration: 1000,
    // Optional: make the animation interruptible by user gestures.
    essential: true   // true = respects reduced‑motion preferences
  };
}

// ---------------------------------------------------
// 3️⃣ Fly function – called on button click
// ---------------------------------------------------
function flyToSanFrancisco() {
  const target = {
    center: [-122.4194, 37.7749], // downtown SF
    zoom: 14,                     // a bit closer than the start
    pitch: 60,                    // tilt a little more for depth
    bearing: 30                  // rotate so streets point NE‑SW
  };

  // Kick off the animation
  map.flyTo(getFlyOptions(target));

  // ---- Accessibility hook (optional) ----
  // Announce the move for screen‑reader users
  const statusEl = document.getElementById('flyStatus');
  statusEl.textContent = 'Map moved to San Francisco';
  // Return focus to the button so keyboard users stay in context
  document.getElementById('flyBtn').focus();
}

// ---------------------------------------------------
// 4️⃣ Wire the button
// ---------------------------------------------------
document.getElementById('flyBtn').addEventListener('click', flyToSanFrancisco);
```

### What the code does

| Step | Reason (cartographic best practice) |
|------|--------------------------------------|
| **`map.flyTo()`** | Keeps the map’s **figure‑ground** (labels, symbols) intact while the camera moves, unlike `jumpTo()` which can disorient users. |
| **`curve` & `duration`** | A gentle easing curve (`0.25`) + 1 s duration feels natural on both desktop and mobile. Adjust `duration` for slower/faster transitions. |
| **Preserve/adjust pitch & bearing** | When you change pitch or bearing you give the user a sense of depth (useful over aerial imagery). If you only need to move the centre, omit those properties and the map will keep the current tilt. |
| **`essential: true`** | Respects the user’s “prefers‑reduced‑motion” setting – the animation will be skipped for users who have asked for minimal motion. |
| **ARIA live region** | Provides a non‑visual cue that the view changed, satisfying WCAG 2.1 accessibility. |
| **Focus management** | After the animation the button regains focus, so keyboard users don’t lose their place in the UI. |

---

## 3️⃣ Tweaking the animation (optional)

| Need | Setting | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| **Longer, cinematic fly** | `duration: 2500, curve: 0.4` | `map.flyTo({…, duration:2500, curve:0.4});` |
| **Instant snap (no animation)** | `duration: 0` | `map.flyTo({center:…, duration:0});` |
| **Zoom‑only change (no pan)** | Omit `center` | `map.flyTo({zoom: 16});` |
| **Fly to a bounding box** | Use `fitBounds` instead of `flyTo` | `map.fitBounds([[west, south], [east, north]], {padding: 40});` |
| **Cancel an in‑progress fly** | Call `map.stop()` before a new `flyTo` | `map.stop(); map.flyTo(...);` |

---

## 4️⃣ Common pitfalls & how the skill helps you avoid them

| Pitfall | Why it happens | Fix (per maplibre‑cartography) |
|---------|----------------|--------------------------------|
| **Labels disappear on imagery** | Using a light‑vector halo on a dark background. | For imagery, always set `text-halo-color: "rgba(0,0,0,0.75)"` and `text-color: "#ffffff"` (see the “Basemap Type Determines Label Colors” table). |
| **Icons blend into the photo** | Full‑color raster icons with no halo. | Use SDF sprites (`sdf: true`) and add `icon-halo-color`/`icon-halo-width` (e.g. dark halo `rgba(0,0,0,0.6)`). |
| **Roads look washed out** | Semi‑transparent road fills over satellite imagery. | Use opaque greys for fills and darker greys for casings (see “Styling Vector Roads Over Imagery”). |
| **Your data layer covers basemap labels** | Adding the layer after the first symbol layer. | Insert your layer **before** the first symbol layer: `map.addLayer(myLayer, firstSymbolId);` |
| **Screen‑reader users miss the change** | No ARIA announcement. | Add an off‑screen live region (`aria-live="polite"`) and update its text after the fly. |

